      "side": 1,
      "message": "#### **Buffer Overflow in `main.c`**\n\nIn `main.c`, you are using `strcpy()` to copy user-provided command-line arguments (`argv[1]` and `argv[2]`) into fixed-size local buffers:\n\n```c\nchar tmp[PATH_MAX];\n// ...\nstrcpy(tmp, argv[2]); \n// ...\nstrcpy(tmp, argv[1]);\n```\n\nCommand-line arguments can exceed `PATH_MAX` (typically 4096 bytes), which will cause a buffer overflow, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution or segmentation faults.\n\n* **Suggested Remediation:** Use `strncpy` (or `strlcpy` if available in your environment) to explicitly limit the copy operation, ensuring the buffer is null-terminated.\n\n```c\nstrncpy(tmp, argv[1], sizeof(tmp) - 1);\ntmp[sizeof(tmp) - 1] \u003d \u0027\\0\u0027;\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 240,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "7c91f2c4e6dfb20882efdf316f4c04799c38715b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
