      "side": 1,
      "message": "#### **Memory Leak in `net_usb.c`**\n\nIn `mbedtls_usb_exist()`, you request a list of devices using `libusb_get_device_list()`. If a target device is found, the loop breaks and the function returns `0`. However, this skips the `error:` label block where `libusb_free_device_list()` is called, resulting in a memory leak every time the device is successfully found.\n\n* **Suggested Remediation:** Ensure the device list is freed on the success path as well.\n\n```c\n        if ((desc.idVendor \u003d\u003d FOCAL_BOOT_VID) /* ... */) {\n            // ... logic ...\n            ret \u003d 0;\n            *vid \u003d desc.idVendor;\n            *pid \u003d desc.idProduct;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Free device list here before returning on success\n    if (usb_ctx \u0026\u0026 usb_ctx-\u003edevs) {\n        libusb_free_device_list(usb_ctx-\u003edevs, 1);\n        usb_ctx-\u003edevs \u003d NULL;\n    }\n    \n    return ret; // Adjust flow so you don\u0027t fall through to error handling unless necessary\n```",
      "range": {
